Key insight: "A test is linked when the spec/adr corpus carries a `([validated by](this#Lnn))` link whose line falls inside the test's line span, or a whole-file link (no `#L`) to the file."

So a link to `validation.test.ts#L7` must fall within the test's line span. If the previous round's spec edit in `hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md` ADDED a link citing `validation.test.ts#L25`... wait no, that's the new test. Hmm.

But wait — where do the OLD tests (7, 13, 19) get their links? From `specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md` presumably, citing `src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L7` etc. Did those line numbers shift? The previous round's diff inserted the import at line 2 (`import type {SessionCursor} ...`), which shifted EVERYTHING below by 1! Look:

```
 import {validateMessage} from './validation.js';
+import type {SessionCursor} from '../../types/sessionStore.js';
```

